WEBVTT

00:00:00.008 --> 00:00:04.647
Perfect lines are useful for learning, but real data is rarely perfect.

00:00:04.647 --> 00:00:08.672
Measurements contain noise. People behave differently.

00:00:08.672 --> 00:00:12.207
Important variables may be missing from the dataset.

00:00:12.207 --> 00:00:18.057
Sensors can contain error. Real processes have natural variation.

00:00:18.057 --> 00:00:25.956
So even when an underlying linear relationship exists, the observations usually do not sit exactly on one line.

00:00:26.406 --> 00:00:29.408
Run the example and look at the scattered points.

00:00:29.408 --> 00:00:34.268
The Linear Regression model still finds a best-fit line through the data.

00:00:34.268 --> 00:00:37.893
Notice that the line does not pass through every point.

00:00:37.893 --> 00:00:45.333
That is expected. The purpose of the model is not necessarily to memorize every training observation.

00:00:45.333 --> 00:00:50.848
It is to capture a useful overall relationship that can generalize to new data.

00:00:50.848 --> 00:00:57.588
This difference between fitting patterns and memorizing data becomes very important later in machine learning.
